    "result_text": "The full suite is green (28 tests, 0 failures/errors) and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation for owners, following the existing derived-field pattern in this Spring Boot app.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), documenting the fixed city-to-region mapping.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` to `toOwnerDto` plus a `locality(Owner)` helper that maps `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other (or null) city.\n\nThis mirrors how sibling derived fields (`membershipTier`, `householdId`, etc.) are computed via MapStruct expression mappings, so `locality` appears in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\n**Tests:** `Cp17Tests` (both cases \u2014 known city `Sydney`\u2192`NSW` and an unknown city\u2192`UNKNOWN`) passes, and the full suite of 28 tests is green.",
